Z||000000||DecadenceR||07-10-2001||11:05 AM||||A man was reading the paper when an ad caught his eye: $100 Porsche! New! The man thought that it was very unusual to sell a Porsche for $100, and he thought it might be a joke or a typo. He soon decided it was worth a shot. He went to the lady's house and sure enough, she had an almost brand new Porsche. <P><BR>"Wow!" the man said. "Can I take it for a test drive?" Unlike what he expected, the man found that the car ran perfectly and took it back to the lady's house.<P><BR>"Why are you selling me this great Porsche for only $100?"<P><BR>"My husband just ran off with his secretary, and he told me I could have the house and the furniture as long as I sold his Porsche and sent him the money."<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||07-10-2001||12:37 PM||||Don't know if this one belongs in Ripley's or is just an urban legend.  But I've heard this before.  Supposedly, it actually happened, and she sold the car of $1.  But you know how myths are.  Would be great if it were true.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||07-10-2001||01:10 PM||||I heard about a guy that found a VW camper for sale in the paper - the ad said: "gas eater..."<P> he went to see it - turns out it was a typo - suppose to say, "gas heater"<P> since he was the only one that had come to see the camper he got a great deal on it.<P>I saw an ad for a Schwinn stingray bike - still in the original box for sale in the penny saver - $200.<P>  Those bikes in orginal condition sell for thousands of dollars on ebay - so I had to call em up.<P>  turns out its a brand new repro Schwinn is putting out - they won it in a contest and dont want it.<P>  and they sell new now for about $200.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||07-10-2001||05:53 PM||||A local guy sold an '86 Porsche 911 a few years ago for $86.  They were going through a divorce and the judge ordered his wife to sell his prized Mach 1 Mustang and give him the money.  She either didn't know the value or was just trying to be a ______ and sold it for around $1000.  The Porsche was hers and had the same stipulation.  He decided to sell it for a buck a year.  True story.  I missed out by about 2 hours.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
